From 75a6343272eab2c8e05c066e89a06cfeb82382b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xbox360 Blades <xbox360-blades@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 14:27:14 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 28/51] Gamer pictures: XamReadTile buffer size,
 XamWriteGamerTile, createprofile's pick

- XamReadTile/Ex copied the whole picture into the caller's buffer
  whatever its size; the 2858 dashboard first asks with a 0-byte buffer,
  so a profile with a picture corrupted its heap and hung it. The size is
  now respected (ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_BUFFER with the size, as xam passes the
  buffer size with the request). XamReadTileEx takes its 9th argument, the
  overlapped (xam 818C0640).
- XamWriteGamerTile (a stub) now stores the picture's 64 and 32 pixel
  images in the profile and its gamercard picture key; its arguments are
  (user, title, big id, small id, 0, overlapped) as createprofile calls it.
  The pictures are xam's own (shrdres 64_/32_fffe07d1...), in gamerpics\.
- Create profile: Save Gamer Profile picks a picture as createprofile does
  (RtlRandom(GetTickCount()) % 12, then + 1) and shows it on its gamercard;
  AddXboxLive's Updating profile stores it (90103380 -> XamWriteGamerTile).

